        "original_id": "a05ae3a3-05e1-5530-a341-cdeab4ffd2b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lucy Gichuhi, Bob Day\n- Roles: Senator for South Australia, independent politician, Family First Party member, businessman\n- Organizations: Family First Party, High Court of Australia, Court of Disputed Returns\n- Places: South Australia, Australia\n- Events: 2016 Australian election, special recount on 13 April 2017\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Gichuhi was born on 23 September 1962 and is an Australian politician.\n- Bob Day was born on 5 July 1952 and is an Australian former politician and businessman.\n- Bob Day served as a Senator for South Australia from 1 July 2014 to 1 November 2016.\n- At the 2016 election, Lucy Gichuhi was a Family First Party candidate for the Senate in South Australia.\n- The High Court of Australia, sitting as the Court of Disputed Returns, decided that Bob Day had not been eligible to stand for election.\n- Following that decision, a special recount ordered by the High Court of Australia on 13 April 2017 declared Lucy Gichuhi elected.\n- Lucy Gichuhi became a Senator for South Australia and sits as an independent.",
